Subject: [PATCH 3/6] [compiler-rt] Build the ORC runtime as C++20

The sprt freestanding STL headers the ORC runtime is compiled against use C++20
concepts and requires-clauses unconditionally, which compiler-rt's default C++17
rejects. Raise the standard for this directory only.

diff --git a/compiler-rt/lib/orc/CMakeLists.txt b/compiler-rt/lib/orc/CMakeLists.txt
index b8d1b03b7..bcfcede6d 100644
--- a/compiler-rt/lib/orc/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/orc/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,10 @@
 # Build for all components of the ORC runtime support library.
 
+# The sprt freestanding STL headers this runtime is built against use C++20
+# concepts/requires unconditionally, so build the ORC runtime at C++20 rather
+# than compiler-rt's default C++17 (directory-scoped override).
+set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)
+
 # ORC runtime library common implementation files.
 set(ORC_COMMON_SOURCES
   debug.cpp
